# Planning / source docs — kept local, not published
info.md
design.md
structure.md
claude.md
assets/README.md

# Staging content for the separate GitHub project repos — never part of the
# Pages site. READMEs and prepared assets live here until uploaded elsewhere.
_github-repos/

# Unredacted originals — NEVER publish.
# Contains Escorts Kubota internal R&D data (competitor benchmarking, ram
# specs, a named colleague) and the signed exoskeleton report. Only the
# redacted derivatives under assets/ go live.
_source/

# The loose originals in assets/ that the redacted derivatives were made
# from. Same reason as _source/ above: internal R&D data, and a signed
# report containing other people's names and student ID numbers.
# Listed explicitly so `git add -A` can never publish them by accident.
assets/Input and output kinematics template.png
assets/Input for forces kinematics template Escorts.png
assets/Output image of forces on Loader.png
assets/Kinematics Calculation template.xlsm

# Source reports the case studies were written from. Kept local: they carry
# matriculation numbers and teammates' full names, and two of them still have
# the figure defects the case-study charts correct.
assets/*.pdf
# Word source reports, same reason — and their docProps carry the *authoring*
# teammate's name (Narinder Kaur, Gaurav) even where the body text doesn't.
# A pattern, not a list: the coursework .docx files arrive in batches and an
# explicit list is one forgotten line away from publishing someone's report.
assets/*.docx
# ...except the generated CVs, which the résumé download buttons serve —
# one per language, both produced by scripts/build-cv.sh.
!assets/Navroop-Singh-CV.pdf
!assets/Navroop-Singh-CV-DE.pdf
assets/Quick-hitch coupler.jpeg
assets/My Picture.jpeg
assets/Professional photo.png

# Claude Code tooling — never part of the published site.
# Holds the local dev-server config and any nested git worktrees.
# Without this, `git add -A` could commit an entire worktree into the repo.
.claude/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
*.log
